      "Oaxaca is the most ethnically diverse state in Mexico, home to sixteen officially recognised Indigenous peoples, including the Zapotecs, Mixtecs, Mazatecs and Mixes, who speak dozens of languages. Many villages around the city specialise in a particular craft: black pottery in San Bartolo Coyotepec, woven rugs in Teotitlán del Valle and brightly painted wooden figures called alebrijes in San Martín Tilcajete.",
